# Frontend environment. Copy to `.env.local` (dev) or `.env.production` (the
# single-VPS deploy — see ../.env.production.example and ../nginx/).
#
# Base URL of the FastAPI backend. Three modes:
#
#   1. "same-origin" — the production deployment: Nginx proxies /api on the
#      SAME origin as the page (see ../nginx/balkan-fleet.conf.example).
#      lib/api.ts treats this literally: every call resolves as a plain
#      relative fetch, no host or port at all. Use this in production.
#
#   2. A loopback value like the dev default below — local development, with
#      `next dev` on :3000 and uvicorn on :8001. The session cookie still
#      works across the port gap, because SameSite ignores the port.
#
#   3. A genuinely remote host (e.g. https://api.example.com) is used exactly
#      as written. This is the only mode that keeps the in-memory Bearer-token
#      fallback alive, because the cookie cannot follow cross-site.
#
# Note this value is inlined by Next at BUILD time, so a production build must
# be made with it already set to "same-origin".
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8001
